From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Demitri Nava <demitri@boltz.bio>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:04:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bes: report target events only for requested targets

Every analysed target got a TargetConfigured, so BuildBuddy listed each
dependency as a target, and showed every dependency whose actions hit the
cache as still building.

As Bazel does, give TargetConfigured and TargetComplete only to the targets a
build, test or install command's resolved patterns name; the next progress
event announces a dependency's action events. A requested target that a
successful command did not build closes as Aborted, SKIPPED.
